WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:16.621
Rose and Oliver were soon convinced that they would learn nothing more that night.

2
00:00:17.662 --> 00:00:18.762
They were about to bid Mrs.

3
00:00:18.822 --> 00:00:19.963
Maylie good night when Mr.

4
00:00:20.003 --> 00:00:21.523
Brownlow and Monks entered the room.

5
00:00:22.664 --> 00:00:24.004
Oliver clutched Rose's arm.

6
00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:24.744
"It's him!

7
00:00:25.745 --> 00:00:26.925
The man I saw at the inn!

8
00:00:28.006 --> 00:00:30.227
The man who later peered in my window with Fagin!"

9
00:00:31.287 --> 00:00:33.248
Monks cast a look of hatred at Oliver.

10
00:00:34.316 --> 00:00:36.757
"This is a painful task for everyone," said Mr.

11
00:00:36.777 --> 00:00:40.079
Brownlow, "but Oliver needs to know about his family."

12
00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.701
Mr. Brownlow pulled Oliver to him and addressed Monks.

13
00:00:43.721 --> 00:00:46.963
"As you know, this child is your half brother.

14
00:00:48.084 --> 00:00:51.546
He is the son of your father and Agnes Fleming, who died giving birth to him."

15
00:00:52.726 --> 00:00:53.887
Oliver's eyes widened.

16
00:00:53.907 --> 00:00:56.449
"That man is my brother?"

17
00:00:56.469 --> 00:00:58.890
"Yes," said Mr.

18
00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:04.225
Brownlow. "His name is Edward Leeford, although he usually goes by 'Monks.'

19
00:01:05.385 --> 00:01:06.665
Tell us what happened to your father."

20
00:01:06.685 --> 00:01:10.926
"My father, Edwin Leeford, was taken ill in Rome," said Monks.

21
00:01:10.947 --> 00:01:15.288
"My mother, from whom he had long been separated, took me there to see him.

22
00:01:16.468 --> 00:01:19.349
After he died, we found a will and a letter addressed to Agnes."

23
00:01:19.369 --> 00:01:21.670
"And what did the letter say?

24
00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:23.770
Did he know he was dying?"

25
00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:24.591
asked Mr.

26
00:01:24.611 --> 00:01:26.371
Brownlow. "Yes.

27
00:01:27.551 --> 00:01:29.352
He begged Agnes not to curse his memory.

28
00:01:30.484 --> 00:01:33.527
And he reminded her of the day when he gave her a ring and a locket with her

29
00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:34.328
first name on it.

30
00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:38.551
There was space left for her last name because he had planned to marry her.

31
00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:41.734
He begged her to always wear it next to her heart."

32
00:01:41.754 --> 00:01:43.456
"And the will?"

33
00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:44.236
said Mr.

34
00:01:44.276 --> 00:01:46.418
Brownlow as Oliver's tears fell fast.

35
00:01:47.559 --> 00:01:48.460
Monks was silent.

36
00:01:49.541 --> 00:01:50.782
Mr. Brownlow spoke for him.

37
00:01:50.802 --> 00:01:56.327
"The will described the miseries his wife had brought upon him and the evil deeds that you had

38
00:01:56.367 --> 00:01:57.428
done from a young age.

39
00:01:58.536 --> 00:02:00.917
He left you and your mother eight hundred pounds each.

40
00:02:02.077 --> 00:02:05.978
The bulk of his property he divided between Agnes Fleming and their unborn child."

41
00:02:07.058 --> 00:02:08.899
But the will had an unusual provision.

42
00:02:08.919 --> 00:02:14.080
"If the child were a girl, she would inherit the money unconditionally," said Mr.

43
00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:19.182
Brownlow. "But a boy would only inherit the money as long as he had never committed a crime.

44
00:02:20.302 --> 00:02:22.883
If he became a criminal, then the money would come to you."

45
00:02:24.023 --> 00:02:25.143
Monks picked up the story.

46
00:02:25.163 --> 00:02:27.964
"My mother burned this will and the letter.

47
00:02:29.096 --> 00:02:31.938
Meanwhile Agnes' father was filled with shame at her pregnancy.

48
00:02:32.999 --> 00:02:37.322
He changed his name and fled to Wales with Agnes and his other daughter, who was much younger.

49
00:02:38.523 --> 00:02:39.923
One night Agnes disappeared.

50
00:02:41.004 --> 00:02:45.427
Her father searched for her but finally stopped, assuming that she'd killed herself to hide her shame.

51
00:02:47.168 --> 00:02:49.810
His heart was broken, and soon afterward he died."

52
00:02:50.891 --> 00:02:51.811
The room was silent.

53
00:02:51.831 --> 00:02:54.413
"Years after this," Mr.

54
00:02:54.433 --> 00:02:58.196
Brownlow said to Monks, "your mother came to see me because she was looking for you.

55
00:02:59.256 --> 00:03:02.439
When you were 18, you robbed her of jewels and money and fled to London.

56
00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.602
There you associated with the lowest outcasts of society.

57
00:03:07.763 --> 00:03:10.405
Ultimately you were reunited with your mother on her deathbed."

58
00:03:11.486 --> 00:03:13.307
Monks crossed his arms over his chest.

59
00:03:13.327 --> 00:03:18.031
"My mother never believed that Agnes killed herself and her unborn child.

60
00:03:19.172 --> 00:03:23.115
She felt that a male child had been born, and I vowed to track down this boy."

61
00:03:24.216 --> 00:03:28.720
Mr. Brownlow explained to the terrified group that Fagin had been one of Monks' old accomplices.

62
00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:34.342
Monks had given Fagin a large reward for keeping Oliver ensnared in a life of crime.

63
00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:40.063
But Fagin had to return some of this reward to Monks if Oliver were ever rescued.

64
00:03:41.124 --> 00:03:44.105
A dispute over this led the two men to the Maylies' country house.

65
00:03:45.405 --> 00:03:48.546
Oliver shuddered at the memory of their faces peering into his window.

66
00:03:48.566 --> 00:03:52.067
"Tell us what became of the locket and ring," said Mr.

67
00:03:52.108 --> 00:03:53.208
Brownlow, turning to Monks.

68
00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:55.260
"I bought them from Mrs.

69
00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:59.542
Bumble, the matron of the workhouse, who had stolen them from the nurse, Sally, who had stolen them

70
00:03:59.562 --> 00:04:00.943
from Agnes after she died.

71
00:04:02.083 --> 00:04:05.004
Then I tossed them in the river, destroying proof of the boy's existence."

72
00:04:06.305 --> 00:04:07.545
"Now, young lady," Mr.

73
00:04:07.585 --> 00:04:08.486
Brownlow said to Rose.

74
00:04:08.506 --> 00:04:11.227
"Give me your hand, and don't tremble.

75
00:04:12.327 --> 00:04:14.828
You need not fear the few remaining words we have to say."

76
00:04:14.848 --> 00:04:20.010
"If they have anything to do with me," said Rose, "I don't have the strength to hear them

77
00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:22.331
now." Mr.

78
00:04:22.351 --> 00:04:23.792
Brownlow drew her arm through his.

79
00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:26.181
"You are stronger than you think."

80
00:04:27.282 --> 00:04:28.263
Then he addressed Monks.

81
00:04:28.283 --> 00:04:30.664
"Do you know this young lady, sir?"

82
00:04:30.684 --> 00:04:34.307
"Yes, I have seen her often," replied Monks.

83
00:04:34.327 --> 00:04:37.750
"I have never seen you before," Rose said faintly.

84
00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:42.193
"The father of the unhappy Agnes had two daughters," said Mr.

85
00:04:42.233 --> 00:04:44.975
Brownlow. "What became of the younger one?"

86
00:04:46.036 --> 00:04:51.139
"The father died far away from any relatives, so a poor, elderly couple took the girl in," said

87
00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:57.007
Monks. "My mother was filled with hatred for any relative of Agnes', so she tracked down the child

88
00:04:57.087 --> 00:04:58.788
and told the couple all about Agnes.

89
00:04:59.969 --> 00:05:03.151
My mother also made up a story that the younger girl was illegitimate.

90
00:05:04.412 --> 00:05:07.935
Soon after that the old couple died, and a widow lady took in the girl."

91
00:05:07.955 --> 00:05:10.837
"Do you see the girl now?"

92
00:05:11.197 --> 00:05:11.597
asked Mr.

93
00:05:11.617 --> 00:05:14.900
Brownlow. "Yes, she's leaning on your arm."

94
00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:19.082
Mrs. Maylie rushed to Rose as the young lady began to faint away.

95
00:05:19.102 --> 00:05:21.024
"My dear girl!

96
00:05:22.132 --> 00:05:27.194
I called you my niece for propriety's sake, but you are and always will be my dearest companion."

97
00:05:27.214 --> 00:05:31.616
"My heart will burst," cried Rose, clinging to Mrs.

98
00:05:31.656 --> 00:05:34.397
Maylie. "I cannot bear all this."

99
00:05:35.638 --> 00:05:36.518
Oliver rushed to her.

100
00:05:36.538 --> 00:05:40.120
"You are my mother's sister, so you are my aunt!"

101
00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:44.381
As they embraced, there was a knock at the door, and Harry Maylie entered.

102
00:05:44.401 --> 00:05:48.163
"I know everything," he said, rushing to Rose's side.

103
00:05:48.183 --> 00:05:50.684
"Mr. Brownlow told me yesterday.

104
00:05:51.744 --> 00:05:54.666
Please allow me to address you on the subject of marriage once more."

105
00:05:54.686 --> 00:05:58.809
"These disclosures do not change my position in relation to yours."

106
00:05:58.829 --> 00:06:01.551
"But I have changed.

107
00:06:02.692 --> 00:06:05.955
I have decided to forsake the world of politics where people might scorn you.

108
00:06:07.116 --> 00:06:09.798
Instead I will be a minister and hope that you will be my wife."

109
00:06:10.958 --> 00:06:12.399
And indeed that is what happened.

110
00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:15.202
Rose and Harry were married and Mrs.

111
00:06:15.262 --> 00:06:18.104
Maylie came to live with them in their little cottage next to the church.

112
00:06:19.316 --> 00:06:22.359
Mr. Brownlow adopted Oliver and they went to live near the Maylies.

113
00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:27.303
Although Oliver was entitled to all of his father's fortune, he agreed when Mr.

114
00:06:27.323 --> 00:06:29.145
Brownlow suggested he split it with his brother.

115
00:06:30.266 --> 00:06:32.948
Unfortunately Monks soon squandered the money and died.

116
00:06:34.049 --> 00:06:37.052
Oliver continued to live happily, watched over by Mr.

117
00:06:37.092 --> 00:06:38.033
Brownlow, Mrs.

118
00:06:38.093 --> 00:06:39.875
Bedwin, and the spirit of his mother.

119
00:06:41.036 --> 00:06:45.600
At last the orphan Oliver Twist had found a home and a family.
